225746	225885	225672	225672	she	93	" The very air feels too heavy to breathe . The cottages , and even the better houses , appear to my eyes damp and weather - stained on the outside , and silent within . The children sit shivering on the thresholds -- do not they?--instead of shouting at their play as they did . Every one looks discontented , and complains -- the poor of want of bread , and every one else of hard times , and all manner of woes , that one never hears of in prosperous seasons . Mr James says the actions for trespass are beyond all example ; Mr Tucker declares his dog , that died the other day , was poisoned ; and I never pass the Green but the women are even quarrelling for precedence at the pump . "
